.TH @APP@ 1 "2026" "@APP@ @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@APP@ \- WhatsApp in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @APP@
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR \fIwhatsmeow\fR|\fIbaileys\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR]
.br
.B @APP@
\fB\-\-doctor\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR \fINAME\fR]
.br
.B @APP@
\fB\-\-update\fR | \fB\-\-reinstall\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.br
.B @APP@
\fB\-\-encrypt\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR] | \fB\-\-decrypt\fR | \fB\-\-change\-passphrase\fR
.br
.B @APP@
\fB\-\-backup\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-with\-media\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-login\fR]
.br
.B @APP@
\fB\-\-restore\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.br
.B @APP@
\fB\-\-version\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
.B @APP@
\fBsend\fR \fICHAT\fR \fITEXT\fR... | \fBsend\fR \fICHAT\fR \fB\-\fR
.br
.B @APP@
\fBtail\fR [\fICHAT\fR...] [\fB\-\-json\fR] | \fBunread\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] | \fBstatus\-line\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR \fIF\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @APP@
is a terminal WhatsApp client. It links to your phone like WhatsApp Web,
stores chats locally in SQLite, and supports notifications, voice notes,
media with inline previews (including the pages of PDFs), replies,
reactions, edits, deleting for you or for everyone, full-text search,
an emoji picker with emoticons turned into emoji as you type, profile
pictures, contact and group details, blocking, chat export, a prompt for
incoming voice calls (declined in tawk or answered on the phone),
per-chat themes and tones, soft-locked chats, editing your own name, about
text and photo, viewing statuses (kept in an archive for
\fBstatus_keep_days\fR) and posting them (whatsmeow only), photos and videos
from the camera, slash commands and an idle screensaver. It reconnects
by itself when the network adapter changes. On first run a wizard links it with a QR code or a
phone-number pairing code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Use this configuration file instead of ~/.config/@APP@/config.ini.
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " NAME"
\fBwhatsmeow\fR runs the WhatsApp protocol in-process (default);
\fBbaileys\fR runs it in a Node.js sidecar.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Write verbose diagnostics to the log files.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check the setup and exit: the terminal (TERM, UTF\-8 locale, colours),
the config file, data folder, themes and emoji list, the WhatsApp backend,
ffmpeg, the audio tools, a media viewer, the PDF page tools (pdftoppm and
pdfinfo from poppler), the screensaver command and whether the chats are
encrypted.
Missing items are printed with a hint on how to install them. The
database is not opened, no file is written and nothing connects to WhatsApp.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Install the newest version from GitHub where this copy is installed, with
the same backends. When this build's commit is already the newest, it says
so and stops. Otherwise it shows the installed version and the newest
commit and asks first; \fB\-\-yes\fR skips the question.
.TP
.B \-\-reinstall
Like \fB\-\-update\fR, but installs even when already up to date. The installer script is
downloaded to a private temporary file, run and removed.
.TP
.B \-\-encrypt
Encrypt your chats (the database) with a passphrase, asked twice. From then
on @APP@ asks for it every time it starts, before the screen is taken over.
There is no way to recover the chats without it. Unencrypted copies kept
before database upgrades are offered for removal; \fB\-\-yes\fR removes them
without asking. Needs a build with SQLCipher. The WhatsApp login stays in
its own unencrypted folder.
.TP
.B \-\-decrypt
Remove the encryption again, after asking for the passphrase.
.TP
.B \-\-change\-passphrase
Change the passphrase: asks for the current one, then the new one twice.
.IP
These three rewrite the database into a new file, check it table by table
against the original and only then replace it; on any failure the original
is left as it was. They refuse to run while @APP@ is running.
.TP
.BI \-\-backup " FILE"
Write a backup of your chats (the database, encrypted or not), settings and
your own themes to \fIFILE\fR, which must not exist yet. The whole file is
encrypted with openssl (AES\-256, PBKDF2) under a passphrase asked twice.
\fB\-\-with\-media\fR adds the media folder; \fB\-\-with\-login\fR adds the
WhatsApp login, which lets whoever has the file and its passphrase use your
account as a linked device.
.TP
.BI \-\-restore " FILE"
Restore a backup after asking (\fB\-\-yes\fR skips the question) and asking
for its passphrase. Every member is checked before anything is extracted;
a backup holding links or paths outside its own folders is refused. What
the restore replaces is kept beside it with a \fB.before\-restore\-\fR
date suffix. Both refuse to run while @APP@ is running.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, with the commit this build came from when it was built
from a git checkout, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
These talk to the @APP@ that is running, over its control socket, when
Settings, Automation, Agent access is on. See CONTROL.md for the protocol
and tawk\-mcp (https://github.com/loganventer/tawk\-mcp) for AI assistants.
A chat is a name, the start of a word in its name, or a phone number.
.TP
.B send \fICHAT\fR \fITEXT\fR...
Send a message; with \fB\-\fR the text is read from standard input.
.TP
.B tail \fR[\fICHAT\fR...] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Print new messages as they arrive, in every chat or those named.
.TP
.B unread \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Print the unread count of each chat.
.TP
.B status\-line \fR[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIF\fR]
Print a short summary for tmux or waybar, such as \(lq💬 3 @1\(rq, or an
empty line when nothing is unread or @APP@ is not running.
\fIF\fR may use {unread}, {mentions} and {chats}.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Tab
Cycle focus between the chat list, messages and the input line.
.TP
.B Enter
Open a chat, send a message, or open the selected media.
.TP
.B Shift+Enter\fR or \fBAlt+Enter
Start a new line in the input or the status composer. Where the terminal
sends Shift+Enter like Enter, bind it to send \fB\\e[13;2u\fR.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Search messages in every chat.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F\fR or \fB/
Filter the chat list by name (\fB/\fR in the chat list).
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Jump to the next chat with unread messages.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Open the emoji picker.
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Attach a file. The \fB+\fR in the input also offers to take a photo or
record a video with the camera (also \fB/camera\fR).
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Record a voice note; Enter sends it and Esc discards it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Collapse or expand the chat list.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Toggle do not disturb.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Start the screensaver.
.TP
.B Alt+V
Attach the picture on the clipboard (also \fB/paste\fR).
.TP
.B Alt+T
Show the transcripts of voice notes in the open chat: as the setting says,
always, or never (also \fB/transcripts\fR). The words come from an agent's
transcriber and are kept in the database.
.TP
.B Ctrl\fR, \fBAlt\fR or \fBShift\fR with \fB\(<-\fR and \fB\(->
In the input, step through what you typed a word at a time. With the up and
down arrows, go to its start or its end.
.TP
.B Alt+L\fR or \fBCtrl+Shift+L
Soft-lock the selected or open chat, or show it again (also \fB/softlock\fR).
The conversation is drawn as shaded shapes until it is shown again.
Ctrl+Shift+L works only where the terminal reports it apart from Ctrl+L.
.TP
.B Alt+O
Chat options: mute, pin, archive, soft lock, chat theme, notification tone,
contact info.
.TP
.B Alt+I
Contact or group details for the selected or open chat (also \fB/info\fR, or
click the name in the title bar): about text, business details, group
description and members, and actions to view the profile picture, search,
soft lock, export the chat with or without media, block or unblock, clear
the chat on this computer, or delete it. Block, clear and delete ask first.
Click the portrait in the title bar to see the picture full size.
.TP
.B Alt+Q\fR, \fBAlt+E\fR, \fBAlt+Shift+E\fR, \fBAlt+M
On a selected message: reply, react, edit, open the message menu.
Typing letters in the chat list searches it; typing on a message writes in the input.
.TP
.B Up
In an empty input: edit your last message, when it is the newest in the chat
and can still be edited.
.TP
.B Ctrl+End
In the input: go to the end of the text; pressed again, scroll the chat to
the newest message. In the conversation: scroll to the newest message.
.TP
.B Delete
On a selected message: delete it for you, or for everyone when it is
yours and recent enough.
.TP
.B Left\fR, \fBRight
On a group header in the chat list: fold or unfold the Pinned or Chats group.
In the viewer: turn the pages of a PDF, then move to the next or previous
item; \fBUp\fR and \fBDown\fR move between items, \fBHome\fR and \fBEnd\fR go to the
first and last page.
.TP
.B d
While a call rings: decline it. Enter or Esc closes the prompt so you can
answer on the phone; tawk cannot carry call audio.
.TP
.B F2
Open the settings panel.
.TP
.B F3
Switch between the Chats and Agentic tabs: requests from agents to
answer, who is connected, the log and permissions.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.PP
Type
.B /help
in the input line for the list of slash commands, such as
.BR /search ,
.BR /mute ,
.BR /theme ,
.BR /tone ,
.BR /softlock ,
.BR /transcripts ,
.BR /info ,
.B /profile
(your name, about text and photo),
.B /status
(post a status),
.B /statuses
(see statuses)
and
.BR /screensaver .
In the header, click your name for your profile, \fB+\fR to post a status
and the circle to see statuses.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/@APP@/config.ini
Settings, also edited from the settings panel.
.TP
.I ~/.config/@APP@/themes/
Your own JSON themes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/@APP@/
Chat database and WhatsApp login.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/@APP@/media/
Downloaded media, with video frames, rendered PDF pages and profile
pictures; safe to delete.
.TP
.I ~/Downloads
Where Save to Downloads copies files and chat exports are written, unless \fBdownload_dir\fR or
XDG_DOWNLOAD_DIR names another folder.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/@APP@/
Log files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a normal exit, 1 when tawk cannot start (for example when the
database cannot be opened).
With \fB\-\-doctor\fR, 1 when something required is missing and 0
otherwise. The commands exit with 0 when done, 1 when something failed, 2
when the request was declined, not allowed or not answered, and 3 when no
@APP@ is listening. 2 for an unknown option or when no interactive terminal is
attached.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME and XDG_STATE_HOME move the
folders above. XDG_DOWNLOAD_DIR sets the downloads folder when
\fBdownload_dir\fR is empty. XDG_RUNTIME_DIR holds the control socket
(\fBtawk/control.sock\fR); TAWK_CONTROL_SOCKET names another path for it.
